WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:07.966
Hey, I saw your post.
I'm here to help.

00:00:08.342 --> 00:00:11.094
Every time you think you have
Cory figured out, you're wrong.

00:00:12.262 --> 00:00:15.265
Here Laura Peterson has told
her to abandon her family,

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:17.601
that they're dragging
her down. And here's Cory

00:00:17.768 --> 00:00:20.103
in her moment of need saying
"no no no no your

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:22.564
family is all that matters, and
I'm gonna help you find him."

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.858
I think it's gonna
create for Bradley

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:27.778
a crisis and it's these
catastrophic events

00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:29.613
that really push
people together.

00:00:30.656 --> 00:00:31.657
I love you.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:36.245
Cory's overwhelmed
by the feeling of love for her.

00:00:36.245 --> 00:00:38.705
And he's heard this
is what people say

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.540
and so it just comes
out of his mouth.

00:00:40.791 --> 00:00:43.418
It's authentic and it's so
what we've been craving

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:45.671
since we watched them in
season one and we were like

00:00:45.671 --> 00:00:46.922
"kiss her! Kiss her!"

00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:49.132
I love the way that
Kerry wrote it.

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:50.926
She's just a wild
and talented genius.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.428
Daniel, I really need
you to come back.

00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:56.431
Okay well that's very sweet
and very stupid,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:00.602
and very much
appreciated but...I quit.

00:01:01.103 --> 00:01:03.730
The Morning Show is really
trying to tell the story of what

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.441
it's like to be a woman of color
in this level of position

00:01:06.441 --> 00:01:09.111
and how Mia is hoping
to make a difference.

00:01:09.319 --> 00:01:12.322
And so she's very very focused
on dealing with Daniel's

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.283
changes to his own goals.

00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:15.993
Can we just be friends and

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:18.620
not talk about work? For once.

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:19.871
How're you holding up?

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:23.750
I love how Kerry did not make
Daniel and Mia one dimensional.

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.919
I think Mia is probably
the person who is the

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.296
hardest on Daniel this season

00:01:27.546 --> 00:01:30.674
and to then actually come
around to really see

00:01:30.674 --> 00:01:32.926
how they're able to be
human and vulnerable

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.885
with each other at the end.

00:01:33.969 --> 00:01:36.221
I hope that people enjoy
that journey this season,

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:38.056
because I definitely
really enjoyed filming it.

00:01:39.182 --> 00:01:40.767
You know you called Chip right?

00:01:42.019 --> 00:01:43.020
I know.

00:01:43.312 --> 00:01:47.149
Chip and Alex their relationship
reaches an amazing place

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:48.233
at the end of this season.

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.902
It is at once deeply
unhealthy I think

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:53.947
but there's a purity to it
and a beauty to it because

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.033
of how honest they
are with each other.

00:01:56.992 --> 00:01:59.286
The network wants
you on the air tonight.

00:01:59.578 --> 00:02:00.412
I'm sick.

00:02:01.163 --> 00:02:02.039
I know, that's the point.

00:02:02.539 --> 00:02:04.416
I knew Alex was
going to get COVID

00:02:04.416 --> 00:02:05.459
I just thought, woah

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:08.086
this is gonna be interesting
to try to pull this off.

00:02:08.253 --> 00:02:10.630
We did a lot of research
in terms of COVID

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.090
and the effects of COVID.

00:02:12.466 --> 00:02:14.301
Jen had to really go there.

00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:16.720
I'm just hoping I get to go
anywhere Mimi goes

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:17.929
cause she's just my rock.

00:02:17.929 --> 00:02:19.723
This show attracts

00:02:19.723 --> 00:02:21.975
the most amazing directors.

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.602
We are so blessed to have Mimi

00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:25.812
as our captain she's
a real visionary.

00:02:26.021 --> 00:02:29.024
Okay Alex, we are live in 3
minutes, come on let's do this!

00:02:29.024 --> 00:02:30.484
We were inspired by Chris Cuomo

00:02:30.484 --> 00:02:32.694
sharing the fact that
he kept working.

00:02:32.694 --> 00:02:35.072
He had to show up
and do his show every night.

00:02:35.155 --> 00:02:37.783
Or else he was pretty
sure he was gonna die.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.159
Here we go! Here we go! Ready?

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:41.370
Either get on the
Alex Levy train

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:43.330
or just stay at the station.

00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:47.125
There's a beautiful
shift in her.

00:02:47.125 --> 00:02:48.460
Where you just see her sort of

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:52.923
stop apologizing for who she is
because she's a human being.

00:02:53.715 --> 00:02:56.426
We leave her at the
end of season 2 I think,

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.804
very much like
the phoenix rising.

00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:02.516
And I think we'll
be making bold decisions about

00:03:02.516 --> 00:03:04.518
being a person, instead
of a persona.

00:03:05.185 --> 00:03:07.104
I'm looking inward
and asking myself,

00:03:07.104 --> 00:03:08.605
who is it that I
actually wanna be?

00:03:10.232 --> 00:03:12.109
And then I'm looking
in the mirror,

00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:14.194
and I'm asking if that's
actually who I am.

00:03:14.486 --> 00:03:15.946
For the audience at home

00:03:15.946 --> 00:03:18.532
hopefully there's been some
clarity around

00:03:18.532 --> 00:03:20.200
what matters to you
and what doesn't.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.411
And what should matter and
what shouldn't.

00:03:22.411 --> 00:03:23.912
If we're not trying to draw
lessons from that

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:25.914
then we're not alive to the
world we're in.

